2	/**
3	 * dispatch_pr_validation.ts — hand a pull request to validation, from a workflow step.
4	 *
5	 * ## Why a person's command goes through validation rather than straight to the agent
6	 *
7	 * A person commenting `/<agent>` on a pull request is asking for a run, and the run
8	 * they are asking for is a judgement about a commit. Starting it immediately means
9	 * it reads a CI result that does not exist yet -- so it either waits with nothing
10	 * able to wake it, or reviews a commit whose checks have not run. Validation is the
11	 * thing that runs CI and waits, and it already dispatches whoever the result calls
12	 * for.
13	 *
14	 * So every agent start on a pull request goes through it, whoever asked: an agent's
15	 * handoff, a person's comment, and the re-validation after a push. One path, one
16	 * place that knows how to wait.
17	 *
18	 * ## Why the branch is resolved here when it is not passed in
19	 *
20	 * The two agent-side callers push a branch and pass the name they pushed. A person's
21	 * comment carries only a pull request number, so this script has to ask GitHub which
22	 * branch the pull request is from -- and a member can comment on a pull request from
23	 * a FORK, whose head branch is a branch of the fork rather than of this repository.
24	 * The read used to happen inline in the workflow step, which meant the name arrived
25	 * unchecked and `--ref` was handed one this repository does not have (#344). It is
26	 * resolved through the same three gates a `pr` run uses (`lib/pr-head-branch.ts`), and
27	 * a refusal is posted on the pull request in words the person can act on rather than
28	 * left as a red job nobody looks at.
29	 *
30	 * ## What `asked-by-person` changes
31	 *
32	 * Who a FAILED check goes back to. An agent that broke its own pull request fixes
33	 * it; a person who asked for a run is owed the answer themselves, and handing their
34	 * request to an agent would be the machinery deciding on their behalf. See
35	 * `ValidationInput.askedByPerson`.
36	 *
37	 * Usage:
38	 *   dispatch_pr_validation.ts --repo OWNER/REPO --number N [--branch B]
39	 *     [--asked-by-person] [--ask ID] [--commenter LOGIN]
40	 */
